  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "The current best is config_003 (pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) at 0.639 acc / 10.60 GPU-hr. Key evidence: multiprofile >> singleprofile, avgpool > transformer, weighted > concat fusion, and imagenet_vit_l ≈ resnet50 (0.635 vs 0.639) at lower cost (7.02 vs 10.60). The largest remaining uncertainty is whether the RNA encoder matters—pca_n2000 is a simple linear projection, while scgpt is a deep pretrained generative model that may capture richer biological structure. config_006 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) directly tests this by swapping only the RNA encoder in the best-performing architecture, while using the cheaper image encoder. If scgpt improves accuracy, it opens a new optimization axis for the remaining 4 experiments; if not, it confirms PCA sufficiency and we can focus on other factors. Expected cost: moderate (~8–12 GPU-hr), slightly above config_051 due to scgpt forward passes but below config_003 since vit_l is lighter than resnet50."
}

